    "md5": "994e121a9aa687c0e02b1bd0d22646b3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1859,
    "chunk_text": "It is only wishful thinking that any investigation conducted by a committee headed by a government MP into an allegation against one of the ruling party heavyweights will be impartial. Expecting such a probe to help bring a wrongdoer to justice is no less ill-advised than \u2018seeking the help of a female clairvoyant to catch a thief who happens to be her own son\u2019, as the old local saying goes.\n\nThe Yahapalana MPs, representing the UNP, did their utmost to manipulate the COPE process to bolster their contention that there had been no scam. If one of those MPs had been appointed the Chairman of the COPE, they would have been able to achieve their goal with ease. They however succeeded in having the then Prime Minister Ranil Wickremesinghe\u2019s name left out of the COPE report. The UNP and the JVP were on a political honeymoon at that time.\n\nIronically, the JVP had Wickremesinghe arrested, two months ago, for alleged misuse of state funds during his visit to London after securing the presidency with the help of the SLPP. The amount of money he is alleged to have misused in the UK pales into insignificance in comparison to the losses caused by the Treasury bond scams, the economic impact of which is yet to be fully calculated, according to Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya.\n\nIt is hoped that the container PSC will not go the same way as the one appointed by the UPFA government in 2012 to prepare the ground for impeaching the then Chief Justice Dr. Shirani Bandaranayake. The UPFA members of that PSC pandered to the whims and fancies of the Rajapaksas, and their Opposition counterparts voted with their feet, calling the probe a witch-hunt, and nobody took the PSC findings seriously\u2013\u2013and rightly so. That is the fate which befalls all probes, PSC\u2008or otherwise, when they are aimed at furthering the interests of those in power."
