    "md5": "aa19619e596ed6fcc0ebe081a5ca53f4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1760,
    "chunk_text": "HNB crowned Sri Lanka\u2019s Top Corporate Citizen\n\nHNB Managing Director/CEO Damith Pallewatte (right) accepting the Overall Winner: Best Corporate Citizen Award from The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Chairman Krishan Balendra. HNB Vice President \u2013 Services Roshan Fernando, Vice President \u2013 Microfinance Mahinda Senevirathne, EVP/Chief Growth Officer Bimal Perera, Chief Operating Officer Sanjay Wijemanne, SVP/Chief Strategy Officer Priyanka Wijayaratne, SVP/Board Secretary Shiromi Halloluwa; Manager \u2013 Sustainable Business Hemantha Seneviratne, and Assistant Manager \u2013 Sustainable Business Shanel Perera also also present\n\nReceives accolade at Ceylon Chamber of Commerce Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability Awards 2025\n\nCrowned Sri Lanka\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen for 2025; secures seven key wins including Top 10 Corporate Citizen and Finance Sector Award for Best Performance\n\nWins Triple Bottom Line Award \u2013 Economic Sustainability (Profit) for strong, responsible financial performance\n\nClinches Best Project Sustainability Award for \u201cSOLO Podi Podi Business\u201d\n\nRecognised for Economic Contribution in Best Performance and Consistent Commitment and Continuous Improvement categories\n\nHNB PLC last week took centre stage at the Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability Awards (BCCSA), organised by the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce (CCC), after being crowned as the nation\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen for 2025. Reinforcing its reputation as partner in progress to the nation, and a standard bearer of corporate excellence, HNB secured a total of seven major honours at this year\u2019s awards, underscoring the bank\u2019s long-term commitment to Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) excellence and its role in driving inclusive, responsible growth."
  },
