    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "HNB PLC last week took centre stage at the Best Corporate Citizen Sustainability Awards (BCCSA), organised by the Ceylon Chamber of Commerce (CCC), after being crowned as the nation\u2019s Best Corporate Citizen for 2025. Reinforcing its reputation as partner in progress to the nation, and a standard bearer of corporate excellence, HNB secured a total of seven major honours at this year\u2019s awards, underscoring the bank\u2019s long-term commitment to Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) excellence and its role in driving inclusive, responsible growth.\n\nIn addition to being honoured with the overall BCCS Award 2025, HNB was also placed among Sri Lanka\u2019s Top 10 Corporate Citizens of 2025, based on the bank\u2019s long-term sustainability strategy and structured Environment, Social and Governance (ESG) governance model.\n\nThe bank\u2019s recognition under the Triple Bottom Line Awards \u2013 Economic Sustainability (Profit) and the dual honours for Economic Contribution \u2013 under both the Category Award for Best Performance and the Category Awards for Consistent Commitment and Continuous Improvement \u2013 Economic Contribution \u2013 further highlighted HNB\u2019s consistent role in enabling enterprise growth, strengthening the financial system and supporting national development priorities.\n\nFurther cementing its leadership within the industry, HNB was also named Winner \u2013 Sector Award for Best Performance \u2013 Finance Sector, reflecting its sector-leading performance, governance standards and alignment with Sri Lanka\u2019s broader sustainability objectives.\n\nMeanwhile HNB\u2019s pioneering \u2018SOLO Podi Podi Business \u2013 women empowerment through digital literacy\u2019 initiative was adjudged Winner \u2013 Best Project Sustainability Awards in recognition of its impact in supporting women micro-entrepreneurs through digital adoption, financial literacy, building improved resilience at the grassroots of the Sri Lankan economy."
