    "md5": "69cef1ffd9fc90065c7b2997697fab2a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "Uber Eats expands to Chilaw, Wennappuwa & Puttalam\n\nUber Eats, Sri Lanka\u2019s most loved delivery app for food, groceries, and more, is now delivering in Chilaw, Wennappuwa, and Puttalam. This expansion further strengthens Uber Eats\u2019 footprint in Sri Lanka and brings greater convenience and economic opportunity to one of Northwestern Province\u2019s most vibrant communities.\n\nFor Uber Eats, the expansion reflects its ongoing commitment to empowering local economies by connecting small businesses and delivery partners to a wider customer base through its app. It also gives customers in these fast-growing towns more choice, accessibility, and convenience than ever before and creates new earning opportunities for local residents.\n\nThe Northwestern coast is known for its bustling fishing communities and distinctive cuisine ranging from Chilaw\u2019s famous crab curry to Wennappuwa\u2019s street-side kottu and Puttalam\u2019s signature prawn dishes. With Uber Eats, locals can now savour these favourites from trusted neighbourhood restaurants, while visitors exploring the region can enjoy authentic Sri Lankan flavours with just a few taps on the phone.\n\nVarun Wijewardane, Country Manager \u2013 Delivery, Uber Sri Lanka, said: \u201cExpanding to Chilaw, Wennappuwa, and Puttalam marks another exciting step in our journey to serve more communities across Sri Lanka. Our goal is to empower local entrepreneurs, merchants, and delivery partners by connecting them to more demand through Uber Eats. We\u2019re proud to bring more choice and convenience to locals and create real economic opportunity in this region.\u201d\n\nThe latest launch in the Northwestern Province builds on Uber Eats\u2019 rapid growth across Sri Lanka, following recent expansions to Jaffna, Gampola, Matale, Matara, Weligama, Mirissa, and Anuradhapura this year, and the Southern Coast corridor from Galle to Ahangama in December 2024 \u2013 further strengthening Uber Eats\u2019 position as the country\u2019s go-to delivery platform."
