    "md5": "39a1f65f0cf6ee9d4008f8358d1f6d63",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1843,
    "chunk_text": "An opportunity has now presented itself for the people\u2019s representatives, in both Parliament and the local government institutions, to show that they care for the people who pay through the nose to maintain them and vote for them generously. The least they can do for the public at this juncture is to mobilise their rank and file, whose numerical strengths they often brag about, in the disaster-stricken parts of the country and assist in the ongoing rescue and relief operations.\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has asked all MPs to go back to their electorates and oversee the rescue and relief operations. Parliamentary sittings have been cancelled for two days for them to do so. There are more than 8,000 local government members at the grassroots level. They and the MPs, numbering 225, should be able to enlist the support of millions of volunteers to help the disaster victims and clean and repair the flood-affected houses and infrastructural facilities.\n\nWill the political leaders who wrap themselves in the flag and declare that they are ready to lay down their lives for the ordinary people, rise to the occasion?\n\nPresident Dissanayake, Opposition Leader Sajith Premadasa and SLPP National Organiser Namal Rajapaksa should take the lead so that others will be compelled to follow them. Theatrics, such as walking along railroads in shorts and vaulting over barriers at political rallies, are of no use to the public. The \u2018patriotic\u2019 political leaders and their party activists must go among the people in these troubled times. That is the way they can show gratitude to the people. What is needed is action and not rhetoric.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
