    "description": "Condolence message from  High Commissioner of  Pakistan on behalf of Government and people of Pakistan",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Condolence-message-from-High-Commissioner-of-Pakistan-on-behalf-of-Government-and-people-of-Pakistan/56-784995",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764354912.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-29-dailyftlk-546b7e79-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "cf894b082c1073a23136b5683199e5dc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 974,
    "chunk_text": "Condolence message from  High Commissioner of  Pakistan on behalf of Government and people of Pakistan\n\nThe Government and people of Pakistan expressed their deepest solidarity with the Government and people of Sri Lanka in wake of the ongoing severe weather crisis caused by cyclonic conditions and unprecedented heavy rainfall across large parts of country.\n\n\u201cWe extend our heartfelt condolences to families of those who lost their lives and expressed sympathies to thousands of citizens who are displaced.\u201d\n\nGovernment of Pakistan commends efforts of Sri Lankan authorities for proactively working with swift and coordinated response in conducting rescue and relief operations.\n\nPakistan reaffirms its commitment to time tested friendship with Sri Lanka based on mutual respect and shared history and supporting Sri Lanka in challenging times.\n\nPakistan believes that Sri Lanka is a resilient nation and will surely find strength and courage to overcome this tragedy."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-11-29-dailyftlk-a99a1b34",
    "num": "dailyftlk-a99a1b34",
    "date_str": "2025-11-29",
    "description": "India deploys INS Vikrant helicopters for Sri Lanka\u2019s cyclone relief efforts",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/India-deploys-INS-Vikrant-helicopters-for-Sri-Lanka-s-cyclone-relief-efforts/56-784996",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764354946.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-29-dailyftlk-a99a1b34-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "aadaa99b2ff8098a3f6f932ae14c4870",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1183,
    "chunk_text": "India deploys INS Vikrant helicopters for Sri Lanka\u2019s cyclone relief efforts\n\nIndia yesterday deployed helicopters from the aircraft carrier INS Vikrant docked in Colombo, to support Sri Lanka\u2019s rescue and relief operations as Cyclonic Storm Ditwah continues to generate severe weather across the island.\n\nDefence Ministry Secretary Air Vice Marshal Sampath Thuyacontha said the Government formally requested assistance from the Indian warship, including the use of its aircraft, to reinforce ongoing humanitarian efforts.\n\nThe request was submitted to the Indian High Commission in Colombo earlier in the day, he said during a special media briefing.\n\nThuyacontha cautioned that the same adverse weather conditions affecting Sri Lanka are also impacting flight operations of the Indian aircraft. As a result, deployment may be limited depending on the intensity of the storm and prevailing safety conditions.\n\nThe Government is continuing evacuation, rescue and relief measures across multiple districts as rains, gale-force winds and rising floodwaters persist.\n\nIndian naval vessels INS Vikrant and INS Udaygiri also donated materials to aid the ongoing weather crisis relief."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
