    "description": "India extends immediate humanitarian relief to Sri Lanka",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/India-extends-immediate-humanitarian-relief-to-Sri-Lanka/56-784997",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764354985.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-11-29-dailyftlk-0e98f43a-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "68dae606240ef7cae7f5549125c8bc79",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1246,
    "chunk_text": "India extends immediate humanitarian relief to Sri Lanka\n\nResponding swiftly to the emerging humanitarian needs following Cyclone Ditwah, the Government of India has arranged urgent relief assistance to support ongoing Humanitarian Assistance and Disaster Relief (HADR) efforts for the affected families.\n\nThe relief provided so far, includes 4.5 tons of dry rations and 2 tons of fresh rations, consisting of staple foods, packaged and ready-to-eat items, dairy and bakery products, beverages, and other nutritional essentials to meet urgent household needs. In addition other essential survival items were also handed over. These supplies were provided from the Indian Naval Ships INS Vikrant and INS Udayagiri, which are currently in Sri Lanka.\n\nIn this challenging moment, India stands in solidarity with the people of Sri Lanka. Guided by its steadfast commitment to the \u201cNeighbourhood First\u201d policy, India remains fully committed to supporting Sri Lanka during this difficult time. Further assistance will continue to be coordinated in consultation with the authorities of the Government of Sri Lanka as the situation evolves.\n\nIndia reaffirms its unwavering support to help Sri Lanka overcome this natural calamity and recover swiftly."
  },
