    "chunk_text": "Hillary Clinton\u2019s It takes a Village \u2026 deals with the importance of community and collective responsibility in child rearing and development. Inspired by an African proverb, she includes personal anecdotes of her family growing up; reports on child development; and examples of community models to argue that a village\u2019s support is crucial for children to grow into caring and resilient adults. Thus the main theme of the book is that raising a child requires the support of the community, not just their immediate family. This fact is well borne out by our experience. When we grew up \u2013 we meaning our generation and even the next \u2013 we lived in extended families. Many of our children\u2019s generation and modern families are confined to children and their parents only and thus the widespread use of drugs and children nowadays suffering mental instability. We felt so secure and happy with no gadgets of today, particularly social media nonexistent then.\n\nA tenth anniversary edition of It takes a Village was published featuring an updated introduction by the author and a separate picture book version.\n\nThe book is more a historical relation of subtle nuances of life, attitudes and times of American First Ladies. In American Grown Michelle, through the gardens of vegetables etc she created on the vast grounds of the White House, promotes healthy eating across America mainly through home gardens. The light we carry offers practical wisdom and strategies for navigating uncertainty and finding strength in difficult times.\n\n(NOTE: The writer has read none of the books mentioned in the article, but plenty of reviews and articles about them and their authors) Nan\n\nLovers flee as shortcut through Mount Lavinia cemetery is disturbed by \u2018ghosts\u2019\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next t