    "chunk_text": "He explains that \u201cthose who have written about the War so far are those who took part in the War. Since I have never experienced war directly, the characters I have created are fictional. The novel follows them wherever they go. This is not a war novel. This is just the story of the victims of the Eelam War.\u201d\n\nYears later he meets Jenny while travelling across the Thar Desert of in India. \u201cShe was tall, with shades of Turkish or Iranian features. She had raised her black hair high, clipped it on her head. Her underlined eyes occupied a large part of her face. Her red lips were open like a bud blooming at midnight. She wore a Punjabi Salwar and had wrapped the Dupatta around her head, covering her neck. Her waist was narrow, broadening out like a professional dancer.\u201d\n\nSo begins the story of the romance between Asokan and Jenny which unfolds right across pages of the novel; forming the backdrop for a thriller that covers war, intrigue, espionage, love, betrayal and pathos.\n\nThe plot is complex, linking combatants of the Sri Lanka Military and the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam, operatives of Indian and Australian intelligence, love, loyalty and intrigue across two continents. The odyssey of war!\n\nPrima Group Sri Lanka supports National Flood Relief Efforts with over Rs. 300 Million in dry rations\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
