    "md5": "d479254b6c2fdd4063edcd14fd5d65bb",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1940,
    "chunk_text": "Disasters and warship on mercy mission\n\nWarships are behemoths that invoke fear and wreak havoc, whether they are fictitious ones like the Man-of-War in Conrad\u2019s Heart of Darkness, firing cannon indiscriminately on indigenous territory or modern, massive aircraft carriers that project airpower at sea and destroy distant targets. They are obviously designed for combat, but they can serve positive purposes. An aircraft carrier has embarked on a humanitarian mission to save lives and provide disaster assistance, giving a whole new meaning to the deployment of warships.\n\nINS Vikrant, India\u2019s first indigenous aircraft carrier, currently docked in Colombo, has undertaken a humanitarian mission in Sri Lanka, which is struggling to carry out search and rescue operations and distribute relief amidst torrential rains, with rivers overflowing, reservoir bunds bursting and mountains collapsing; tens of thousands of people are crying out for help. Weather disasters have claimed more than 210 lives during the last few days, according to official reports. Hundreds of people have gone missing, and the death toll is rising.\n\nPakistan has also launched a major operation to assist Sri Lanka. Its naval ship PN SAIF, currently on a port call in Colombo, too, has provided relief to the disaster victims and deployed a helicopter for rescue operations. Such assistance will go a long way towards helping the disaster victims. Many other countries have come forward to provide disaster assistance.\n\nIt was heartening to see two choppers from Vikrant, India\u2019s pride, braving inclement weather and doing sorties to save lives in the disaster-stricken areas of this country. Their deployment has stood many disaster victims in good stead. This humanitarian gesture has cast India, often perceived as the Orwellian Big Brother, in the exalted image of Loku Aiya or Periya Anna, the affectionate Sri Lankan term for the caring eldest brother."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
