    "md5": "7d26e2dee92e02b7a93688a1d718b890",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1319,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s .LK domains set for global stage with new partnership\n\nIn a move to put Sri Lanka on the digital map, the LK Domain Registry has teamed up with ShortDot, a global domain specialist, to make .LK domains available worldwide.\n\nThis partnership will leverage ShortDot\u2019s network of over 400 registrars, making it easier for international businesses and individuals to register a .LK address. The strategy includes marketing .LK as a short, modern alternative for \u201clink,\u201d moving beyond its traditional country-code identity.\n\n\u201cThis is a major step in establishing .LK as a globally recognized domain,\u201d said Prof. Gihan Dias of LK Domain Registry. ShortDot brings a proven track record, having helped the .qpon domain grow from a few hundred to over 30,000 registrations in just six months.\n\nThe collaboration aims to boost Sri Lanka\u2019s digital identity, offering the world a new, versatile option for establishing an online presence.\n\nBally\u2019s Colombo marks 30 years, solidifies reputation as a \u2018vibrant leisure hub\u2019\n\nSri Lanka reassures tourists: Island remains safe and open amidst weather conditions\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
