    "description": "Japan PM offers condolences, emergency relief and  sends assessment team",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Japan-PM-offers-condolences-emergency-relief-and-sends-assessment-team/56-785038",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764540863.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-01-dailyftlk-68a6ba96-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f2a62a0bc606a0b6512b40511093e797",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 802,
    "chunk_text": "Japan PM offers condolences, emergency relief and  sends assessment team\n\nJapanese Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi has issued the following statement following the devastating effects of Cyclone Ditwah on Sri Lanka:\n\n\u201cI am deeply saddened by the loss of many precious lives caused by the cyclone that hit Sri Lanka. I express my deep condolences to the victims and the bereaved families.\n\nBased on a humanitarian perspective and in view of our friendly relations with Sri Lanka, Japan has decided to dispatch an assessment team and provide emergency relief goods to support those who are affected by the cyclone through the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).\n\nI offer my sincere prayers for the earliest possible recovery of the injured and the reconstruction of disaster-stricken areas.\u201d"
  },
  {
