    "md5": "d6a17d86b24d02b27378be2deff80fd9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2023,
    "chunk_text": "The Disaster Management Centre (DMC), meanwhile, confirmed that its own estimates\u2014still preliminary\u2014show that the national recovery bill will rise sharply once the full impact on housing, roads, electricity networks, and public assets is tallied.\n\nA senior DMC official told The Island Financial Review that the immediate relief and emergency response phase alone had already consumed a significant portion of the 2025 disaster-relief allocation.\n\n\u201cOnce we add infrastructure rehabilitation and long-term recovery, the total cost will be far higher than the initial agricultural estimate.\u201d\n\nThe official noted that several districts would require complete reconstruction of local bridges, culverts, and riverbank protections\u2014investments that are capital-intensive and slow to complete.\n\nEconomists warn that the combined loss of crops, transport disruptions, and emergency expenditures is likely to trigger short-term inflationary pressure, particularly in rice, vegetables, and essential commodities.\n\nThe Environment Ministry confirmed that significant sections of irrigation networks\u2014key to the upcoming cultivation cycle\u2014need urgent interventions. Any delays, they warn, will deepen agricultural losses and increase reliance on imports.\n\nTreasury sources, though not authorized to speak publicly, indicated that some development and capital projects may be deferred to re-allocate funds to disaster recovery.\n\nBoth the Environment Ministry and the DMC stressed that the recurring nature of climate-driven disasters is now a serious macroeconomic risk.\n\n\u201cOur annual disaster bill is rising. Floods, landslides, and extreme weather events are no longer episodic\u2014they are becoming structural challenges. Unless resilience funding is prioritized, these shocks will continue to erode growth,\u201d a senior ministry official said.\n\nBourse seized by panic-buying of stocks as flood shock persists\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel