    "md5": "d00834ae73e58054cccc81eb9164d4c3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1955,
    "chunk_text": "Seychelles festive scene for Mirage\n\nMusic lovers are going to miss Mirage this festive season. In fact, they were not in town for the festive season last year, too. And the reason for their absence is because the folks at Seychelles crave for the music of Mirage and so they head for the Seychelles to do the needful.\n\nThe band is scheduled to leave for the Seychelles within the next few days and they will be featured at the Hilton Labriz Resort \u2013 the Lo Brizan pub/restaurant.\n\nMirage will be seen in action six nights a week, during the month of December, from 8.00 pm to 11.00 pm, with Christmas Eve, Christmas, and New Year\u2019s Eve being extra special nights.\n\nAccording to reports coming my way, Christmas Eve and New Year\u2019s Eve 2024 were celebrated with much gaiety at the Lo Brizan, with the 31st night celebrations going on till 2.30 am.\n\nMirage made the lead up to the dawning of 2025 extra special with a medley of songs that brought nostalgia to the crowd present and, after \u2018Auld Lang Syne,\u2019 it was music that had everyone gyrating on the dance floor.\n\nThis will be their fourth stint at the Lo Brizan pub/restaurant and the band has turned out to be quite popular with enthusiastic crowds turning up to see them in action.\n\nFrench, German and Russian tourists, and locals, as well, patronise this outlet, and the group caters to these holidaymakers with a repertoire that is made up of songs that include Russian, French and German, and the language spoken in the Seychelles, Creole, with female vocalist Danu being quite adaptive, singing in all four languages.\n\nDonald Pieris: Regarded as one ofSri Lanka\u2019s most iconic vocalists\n\nLocal music lovers will get the opportunity of seeing their favourite band in action again, towards mid-January, after they complete their assignment in the Seychelles.\n\nBack home, they will move into action at their usual venues, in Colombo: Gatz, at Cinnamon Life, and Mamas Beach, in Hikkaduwa."
