    "chunk_size_bytes": 1487,
    "chunk_text": "It is very clear that these cyclone conditions that have occurred in the three ocean regions of the Bay of Bengal, the Strait of Malacca and the South China Sea, within a period of about a week, are giving the countries in the tropical zone a chance to think about a new trend developing in the weather conditions. It seems that we will have to find out why a cyclone, with such a certain intensity, develops unusually in a cyclone free zone. If this situation starts to emerge again and again, it must be said that it is impossible to prevent the countries in this region from being in danger continuously.\n\nThe increase in the temperature of the equatorial ocean is caused by climate change. As the temperature increases, the evaporation of ocean water increases and the tendency for depressions to occur more frequently increases. These events clearly show that there is a very high probability that such depressions will transform into cyclones. Thus, it is evident that Sri Lanka is no longer safe from cyclones. Therefore, it must be said that the need for conducting timely research with constant attention is strongly felt.\n\nThe writer is Senior Lecturer (Geology), Department of Geography, University of Colombo\n\nA national and international partnership catalysed by a national tragedy\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
