    "num": "dailyftlk-ea7e3f8d",
    "date_str": "2025-12-02",
    "description": "\u201cMaldivians with Ceylon\u201d telethon extended as donations hit Rs. 255 m",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Maldivians-with-Ceylon-telethon-extended-as-donations-hit-Rs-255-m/56-785113",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764627421.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-02-dailyftlk-ea7e3f8d-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "7e10b2981763a10f51d6765c07cbb275",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1421,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cMaldivians with Ceylon\u201d telethon extended as donations hit Rs. 255 m\n\nThe \u201cMaldivians with Ceylon\u201d telethon was extended till 2 p.m. yesterday after drawing an overwhelming nationwide response to support Sri Lanka, which is facing severe destruction, displacement and fatalities caused by heavy rains linked to storm Ditwah. Public Service Media announced the extension to allow more citizens and institutions to contribute.\n\nThe telethon began at 9 a.m. on Sunday morning and was initially scheduled to end at 1 a.m. However, donations surged throughout the day as State institutions, Government-owned companies, private sector firms and members of the public rallied behind the cause, prompting organisers to extend the duration.\n\nAccording to the latest update, the telethon had now raised MVR 11,015,854.65 and $ 48,681.31, which amounts to about Rs. 255 million in total contributions for Sri Lanka.\n\nThis marks one of the most significant humanitarian mobilisations in the Maldives, underscoring the deep and longstanding ties between the two countries.\n\nDonations remain open in both currencies through QR payments, cash, cheques, bank transfers and collection boxes placed across Mal\u00e9, Hulhumal\u00e9 and Villimal\u00e9.\n\nWith the extension in place, the \u201cMaldivians with Ceylon\u201d telethon continues to unite communities across the Maldives in a powerful show of solidarity during Sri Lanka\u2019s time of need."
  },
