    "chunk_text": "After all, mountains have no voices, forests have no votes, and rivers cannot protest. Yet, growth that destroys nature is the most unsustainable, the riskiest, the deadliest of all negative growth types. Years, even decades of economic and other achievements can be wiped out by one natural catastrophe. As we are experiencing today. Where we go from here depends on whether \u2013 or not\u2013 we continue to be possessed by the goal of high growth without bothering to count its socio-political, human, and environmental cost\n\nThe horrific tragedy we are living through is the climatic equivalent of the economic collapse of 2022. The consequences though will be way more extensive both in scale and depth and far-reaching."
