    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a34b205e011e4a3a5d874e735a518755",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1339,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka moves toward electronic invoicing with RAMIS upgrade\n\nThe Cabinet of Ministers on Monday approved engaging with Singapore-based NCS Solutions Ltd., to upgrade the Revenue Administration Management Information System (RAMIS) of the Inland Revenue Department.\n\nThe upgrade will introduce a Web API facility for VAT-registered individuals, marking a key step toward modernising tax administration.\n\nAlthough Sri Lanka has not yet implemented a real-time electronic invoicing system, many countries are adopting such frameworks to enhance tax transparency, curb evasion, and streamline business transactions.\n\nIn line with these global trends, the Inland Revenue Department has evaluated the introduction of an electronic invoicing system integrated with RAMIS.\n\nThe evaluation concluded that implementing a secure Web Application Programing Interface (Web API) would serve as the initial stage of this transition, enabling VAT-registered taxpayers to interface more efficiently with the department\u2019s digital tax systems.\n\nThis initiative aligns with broader efforts to modernise the country\u2019s tax administration and improve compliance through technology-driven solutions.\n\nThe proposal to this effect was presented by President Anura Kumara Dissanayake in his capacity as the Finance, Planning and Economic Development Minister."
  },
