    "md5": "467c0ce3cae49d052ba6dd338c7fcace",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1462,
    "chunk_text": "TMC sets stage for transformative growth with Northern Investment Summit\n\nTo build groundwork for transformative initiative, TMC delegation visits Northern Province engaging in high-impact meetings and fostering strong public\u2013private collaboration\n\nThe Management Club (TMC) has announced the Northern Investment Summit (NIS), a landmark initiative in January 2026 aimed at unlocking the full potential of the Northern Province and positioning it as one of the country\u2019s most promising investment frontiers.\n\nThe Summit\u2019s core purpose is to generate widespread awareness of the region\u2019s immense potential, attract both local and foreign investors and create a unified platform for dialogue between Government Authorities, State Agencies, Investors and local stakeholders.\n\nBy spotlighting key development sectors such as Agriculture and Fisheries, Education, IT and Technology, Tourism, Retail and Energy, NIS aims to catalyse sustainable growth while enabling the infrastructure, logistics support and SME empowerment necessary to drive long-term transformation. Equally important is the emphasis on aligning manpower capacity with future industry requirements through targeted skill development and capacity building\u2014ensuring the people of the North are fully prepared to participate in the region\u2019s emerging opportunities.\n\nA central strength of the NIS initiative is its alignment with the Government of Sri Lanka\u2019s national development vision."
  },
