    "chunk_size_bytes": 1302,
    "chunk_text": "By spotlighting key development sectors such as Agriculture and Fisheries, Education, IT and Technology, Tourism, Retail and Energy, NIS aims to catalyse sustainable growth while enabling the infrastructure, logistics support and SME empowerment necessary to drive long-term transformation. Equally important is the emphasis on aligning manpower capacity with future industry requirements through targeted skill development and capacity building\u2014ensuring the people of the North are fully prepared to participate in the region\u2019s emerging opportunities.\n\nA central strength of the NIS initiative is its alignment with the Government of Sri Lanka\u2019s national development vision.\n\nFurther alignment has come from the Sri Lanka Tourism Development Authority, the Department of Agriculture, the Department of Fisheries, the Coconut Development Authority, the Urban Development Authority (UDA), the Industrial Development Board (IDB) and the Foreign Affairs Ministry \u2014each reinforcing national-level commitment to making NIS a cornerstone of regional economic renewal.\n\nTo build the groundwork for this transformative initiative, a dedicated TMC delegation visited the Northern Province from 16 to 19 November 2025, engaging in high-impact meetings and fostering strong public\u2013private collaboration."
