    "md5": "ce3973be1f847eecc65e1c0ef2cab4c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1823,
    "chunk_text": "To build the groundwork for this transformative initiative, a dedicated TMC delegation visited the Northern Province from 16 to 19 November 2025, engaging in high-impact meetings and fostering strong public\u2013private collaboration.\n\nThe team engaged in constructive discussions with Business Chambers of Jaffna, as well as with the Government Agents of Jaffna, Mullaitheevu, Kilinochchi, Mannar and Vavuniya. These meetings focused on identifying development bottlenecks, understanding local strengths, exploring investment readiness and establishing long-term collaborative frameworks essential for successful implementation of the Northern Investment Summit. The reception was overwhelmingly positive, with each stakeholder expressing enthusiasm and confidence in the project\u2019s long-lasting value to the region.\n\nThe outcomes of the visit were exceptional, forging a series of high-level partnerships and endorsements that will form the backbone of the Summit\u2019s success. A shared vision emerged\u2014one that integrates public sector leadership, private sector drive, and local community engagement to redefine the Northern Province\u2019s economic trajectory.\n\nThe Northern Investment Summit stands as a testament to TMC\u2019s enduring commitment to national development. Through this initiative, the organisation continues its legacy of empowering industries, developing leaders, inspiring innovation and championing inclusive growth across the country. It represents one of TMC\u2019s most ambitious national-level contributions\u2014designed to build a more connected, competitive and prosperous Sri Lanka.\n\nAs preparations for the Northern Investment Summit gather momentum, the outcomes of the November visit have already ignited a wave of anticipation and renewed interest among investors, industry leaders and policymakers."
