    "chunk_text": "At the strategic level, India\u2019s Operation Sagar Bandhu should be viewed in the larger context of the 7th National Security Adviser level meeting of the Colombo Security Conclave held in New Delhi November 20, roughly a week before the weather turned virulent in Sri Lanka. Member States including Maldives, Mauritius, Sri Lanka and Bangladesh at the Conclave hosted by India. Seychelles participated as an observer was admitted as a full member at the meeting. Malaysia attended the meeting as a Guest.\n\nChina will take note of Operation Sagar Bandhu as it has demonstrated an operational framework for assistance. The same applies probably to Turkiye, which is taking baby steps to build a naval coalition with Pakistan and Maldives.\n\n*Col R Hariharan VSM, a retired MI specialist on South Asia and terrorism, served as the head of intelligence of the Indian Peace Keeping Force in Sri Lanka 1987-90. He is associated with the Chennai Centre for China Studies."
