    "chunk_size_bytes": 1889,
    "chunk_text": "One choice is for the majority of the Southern countries to align with states within their grouping who are leading democracies and notable \u2018Swing States\u2019; that is, democratic countries that wield tangible power and influence in the councils of the world. Two such states are India and South Africa. The latter\u2019s voice cannot be easily overlooked by the big powers since they wield decisive influence in international affairs.\n\nThe Donald Trump administration, which is no respecter of environmental concerns, should be compelled by a reunited, revitalized South to see that it would be in the interests of the US and the West to ensure the well-being of the developing world. For instance, how could there be sustained and sizeable markets in the South for Western goods and services, if Southern underdevelopment is perpetuated as a result of frequently occurring environmental debacles and wars?\n\nBesides, the US and other major military powers of the West need to be made to perceive that durable peace within their borders would only be possible if the wars and conflicts of the world are peacefully resolved. For instance, illegal migration is an explosive political issue in many Western states. Such migration is a result, among other factors, of ongoing conflicts and wars within Southern countries and Western arms sales are instrumental in keeping these conflicts raging. There is no escaping the conclusion that a thriving and uncontrolled arms industry would be in the interests of none. There is no alternative as well to the facilitation of peace worldwide by the major powers of the North and South.\n\nWhen the Waters Rise: Floods, Fear and the ancient survivors of Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
