    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f6af43ef076079c5250877c450ff5f8d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1626,
    "chunk_text": "Binance Charity\u2019s contribution will be allocated toward life-saving relief essentials, including food supplies, clean drinking water, hygiene and dignity kits, medical supplies, emergency medical assistance, and temporary shelter materials as well as providing cash grants for the most vulnerable communities. This support aims to ease the immediate burden on displaced families and help accelerate recovery efforts in the hardest-hit districts.\n\nSri Lanka Red Cross Society Secretary General Dr. Mahesh Gunasekara said: \u201cCyclone Ditwah has created an unprecedented humanitarian challenge, leaving thousands in urgent need of assistance. The Sri Lanka Red Cross Society is fully mobilised on the ground, providing life-saving support and helping affected communities regain stability. We sincerely appreciate the generous contribution from Binance Charity, which strengthens our capacity to respond swiftly and effectively. Strategic partnerships of this nature are critical to delivering timely relief and supporting the recovery of the most vulnerable to build back better.\u201d\n\nThe cyclone has severely affected the country, resulting in extensive flooding, infrastructure collapse, and widespread displacement. With a significant portion of the population still in shelters and facing heightened health and safety risks, urgent relief remains critical to restoring dignity, stability, and access to essential services.\n\nMembers of the public wishing to contribute to ongoing relief efforts may do so through the Sri Lanka Red Cross Society\u2019s official donation channels or visit their website: https://www.redcross.lk/"
  },
