    "description": "Harsha says Rebuilding Sri Lanka needs Parliament sanction, oversight",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/news/Harsha-says-Rebuilding-Sri-Lanka-needs-Parliament-sanction-oversight/56-785207",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764809791.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-04-dailyftlk-77c69f10-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c9a782d60121a0f03805c07801f6f57a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1364,
    "chunk_text": "Harsha says Rebuilding Sri Lanka needs Parliament sanction, oversight\n\nSamagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Dr. Harsha de Silva called for Parliamentary approval and oversight over the Rebuilding Sri Lanka initiative.\n\nSpeaking in Parliament yesterday, he said the proposed Rebuild Sri Lanka Fund cannot be created without the approval of the legislature.\n\n\u201cParliament has full control over public finance in terms of the Constitution,\u201d he said. He noted that the Public Financial Management Act does not permit statutory funds to be established at will.\n\n\u201cWe have no objections to establishing the fund. It must be established as per the Constitution and the Public Financial Management Act,\u201d he told the House.\n\nThe Cabinet has already approved the creation of the Fund, which is intended to mobilise resources from both the public and private sectors for the rehabilitation of essential infrastructure, including highways, irrigation systems, and other facilities damaged by the disaster.\n\nA public-private Management Committee has been appointed to administer the Fund, set priorities, allocate resources, and ensure transparency in financial operations. The Committee is chaired by Labour Minister and Deputy Minister of Finance and Planning Dr. Anil Jayantha Fernando, with Senior Additional Secretary to the President G.M.R.D. Aponsu serving as Convenor."
  },
