    "md5": "e6fc199a08a72ac7945717d1f6bf1ac3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1709,
    "chunk_text": "Fems\u2019 three-year winning streak at the SLIM Brand Excellence Awards showcases its mission to empower women nationwide\n\nFems, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading feminine care brands, continued its strong performance at the SLIM Brand Excellence Awards 2025, securing three major wins this year. The brand has maintained a consistent presence at the awards for three consecutive years, from 2023 to 2025, earning a series of Gold, Silver and Bronze recognitions across key categories.\n\nIn 2025, Fems received Gold for CSR Brand of the Year and for Innovative Brand of the Year, and secured Bronze for Local Brand of the Year. The accomplishment is a momentous landmark for the brand as Fems becomes the first feminine hygiene brand in Sri Lanka to win Local Brand of the Year, consolidating leadership for its deep local relevance and consumer trust.\n\nFems\u2019 recognition as CSR Brand of the Year, Gold highlights purposeful, impact-driven initiatives truly delivering results. Throughout the years, Fems has demonstrated an unwavering dedication to tackling period poverty and breaking cultural taboos around menstrual health.\n\nAddressing the critical issue of low sanitary napkin usage in Sri Lanka, Fems introduce the affordable \u2018Fems AYA\u2019 range, launching H.E.R. Foundation with three pillars: Help, Empower, and Rise, to fight period poverty, normalize menstruation, and celebrate women overcoming challenges. The brand has educated over 400,000 women and girls engaging schools, factories, plantations, universities, and prisons, extending monthly donation programmes for female inmates. These initiatives demonstrate Fems\u2019 holistic commitment to menstrual health, education, and empowerment islandwide."
