    "chunk_text": "Addressing the critical issue of low sanitary napkin usage in Sri Lanka, Fems introduce the affordable \u2018Fems AYA\u2019 range, launching H.E.R. Foundation with three pillars: Help, Empower, and Rise, to fight period poverty, normalize menstruation, and celebrate women overcoming challenges. The brand has educated over 400,000 women and girls engaging schools, factories, plantations, universities, and prisons, extending monthly donation programmes for female inmates. These initiatives demonstrate Fems\u2019 holistic commitment to menstrual health, education, and empowerment islandwide.\n\nInitiatives such as sanitary napkin dispenser units in public spaces, and educational outreach campaigns challenging long-standing norms, were among the many innovations introduced to keep the Sri Lankan female consumer at heart.\n\nIn addition, the brand continues to expand its product portfolio to meet diverse consumer needs. The new 3X Protection proposition \u2014 offering Leak Proof, Skin Safe, and Body Fit features, further strengthening consumer confidence in the brand. Meanwhile, the Ultra\u2011Thin range caters to personalized needs with a longer and thinner format of pads, ensuring comfort without compromise. Also, the cycle pack that caters to menstrual flow throughout the period days.\n\nSecuring Local Brand of the Year, Bronze is particularly significant, as Fems is the first feminine hygiene brand in Sri Lanka to achieve such a recognition.\n\nDialog Enterprise Principal Sponsor of Sri Lanka CERT National Cyber Security Conference 2025\n\nStudents\u2019 creativity raises voices against illegal migration at Zero Chance Awards\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
