    "num": "dailyftlk-dd101a30",
    "date_str": "2025-12-05",
    "description": "OPA members, associations unite to support those affected by Cyclone Ditwah",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/OPA-members-associations-unite-to-support-those-affected-by-Cyclone-Ditwah/34-785258",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764894597.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-05-dailyftlk-dd101a30-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "6045c35900fcedfcb7376b9615c25c1c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1058,
    "chunk_text": "OPA members, associations unite to support those affected by Cyclone Ditwah\n\nIn the wake of the severe humanitarian crisis brought about by Cyclone Ditwah, the Member Associations as well as the Members of the Organisation of Professional Associations of Sri Lanka (OPA) have come together to extend vital assistance to affected communities. Acting promptly to ensure timely relief, all OPA Members and Member Associations have collectively contributed dry rations, sanitary items, bottled water, and other essential supplies worth over Rs. 1 million to all individuals impacted by this unprecedented disaster. The donations were handed over by the OPA President Jayantha Gallehewa, to the Sri Lanka Rupavahini Corporation (SLRC), Director-General Manoja Nadeeshana Amarasinghe on the 3 December 2025.\n\nThe unwavering support and generosity demonstrated by the Member Associations as well as the Members reflect the strong commitment of the professional community to stand in solidarity with those in need and support the nation during this challenging time."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-12-05-dailyftlk-241fb565",
    "num": "dailyftlk-241fb565",
    "date_str": "2025-12-05",
    "description": "Hutch contributes Rs. 60 m to  support cyclone-affected communities",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/Hutch-contributes-Rs-60-m-to-support-cyclone-affected-communities/34-785259",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764894671.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-05-dailyftlk-241fb565-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "59b83b41b4b5f7fedcba568c55939466",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 906,
    "chunk_text": "Hutch contributes Rs. 60 m to  support cyclone-affected communities\n\nAs part of ongoing relief efforts for communities affected by Cyclone Ditwah, Hutch Sri Lanka has donated Rs. 60 million to the Government\u2019s \u2018Rebuilding Sri Lanka\u2019 Fund. The contribution was officially handed over yesterday at the Presidential Secretariat.\n\nThe donation cheque was presented to Secretary to the President Dr. Nandika Sanath Kumanayake by Hutch officials, including Hutchison Asia Telecommunications Ltd., Hong Kong Project Director/Hutch Director Ann Chen and Hutch Sri Lanka CEO Saumitra Gupta.\n\nIn addition to the financial contribution, HUTCH has actively provided free calls, data and SMS services to those impacted by the cyclone. The company has also deployed mobile charging units and aviation engineers to promptly restore damaged communication towers, ensuring vital connectivity for affected communities."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-12-05-dailyftlk-feb20b55",
    "num": "dailyftlk-feb20b55",
    "date_str": "2025-12-05",
    "description": "CH17 to allocate 10,000 privilege cards to volunteers to mark Ditwah relief and aid",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/CH17-to-allocate-10-000-privilege-cards-to-volunteers-to-mark-Ditwah-relief-and-aid/34-785260",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1764894716.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-12-05-dailyftlk-feb20b55-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f1385b95acaf590792ca5cd3928ed5d8",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1960,
    "chunk_text": "CH17 to allocate 10,000 privilege cards to volunteers to mark Ditwah relief and aid\n\nCH17 has announced plans to issue 10,000 special digital privilege cards to individuals, groups, organisations supporting the ongoing rescue and disaster relief work. Additionally, CH17 has developed a program that could assist agencies who are in control over any type of aid relief work, to monitor on real time basis, the process and to take immediate action should there be shortcomings.\n\nCH17 has launched a special nationwide initiative to honour and support everyone working tirelessly on disaster relief efforts. The program will recognise first responders, donors, volunteers, welfare teams and media personnel who have stepped forward selflessly to help rebuild the country after the cyclone devastation.\n\nCH17 CEO Jumar Preena said, \u201cWe believe our country will rise again, but only if we take the time to recognise those who served first and served hardest. We will open this Privilege Program to all those risking their safety, time, and comfort to support the destitute. Their service is the foundation on which Sri Lanka will rebuild.\u201d\n\nAs part of this initiative, CH17 will issue a simple digital privilege card to registered responders. This electronic card will carry the volunteer\u2019s name and a unique registration number. It will also include a scannable QR code and a 16-digit card number \u2014 just like a payment card number but used only for identity and fairness. When shown at participating stores, it will unlock special discounts funded entirely by merchants who wish to support caregivers.\n\nCH17 partner retailers from closed-group Privilege Networks, have been requested to accept the digital card and extend special discounts to responders during purchases. CH17 will also invite thousands more private merchants, shops and service providers to join this goodwill effort, so more volunteers can be supported in more places across the island."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
