    "md5": "82ebbcdbeaf8421a14c7f3c0fa7a8c78",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1685,
    "chunk_text": "UAE extends urgent humanitarian aid to flood-stricken Sri Lanka\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to United Arab Emirates Arusha Cooray expresses deep appreciation to President Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan, senior officials and multiple organisations\n\nIn a demonstration of solidarity and compassion, the United Arab Emirates has launched an urgent humanitarian response to support Sri Lanka as it deals with devastating floods and landslides. Acting under the directives of President Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan, the UAE has mobilised resources and expertise to assist communities affected by the disaster.\n\nThrough the Joint Operations Command, the UAE Aid Agency, the UAE Red Crescent and UAE\u2019s Urban Search and Rescue have coordinated a swift relief mission, deploying specialised search and rescue teams from the Abu Dhabi Civil Defence Authority. These highly trained professionals, equipped with boats and advanced rescue gear, have joined local responders in locating trapped individuals, evacuating families, and providing critical medical care in the hardest hit regions. Their arrival has brought hope to communities facing challenges.\n\nThe UAE\u2019s response also includes the rapid delivery of emergency relief supplies. Six flights have arrived at Bandaranaike International Airport, Katunayake, up until 4 December operated by the UAE Air Force, one of the world\u2019s largest cargo transport planes. The aircrafts contained temporary housing units, food packs, tents, blankets, mattresses, vehicles for rescue teams, and motorbikes designed to navigate difficult terrain. These supplies are being distributed to displaced families across severely impacted districts."
