    "chunk_text": "The UAE\u2019s response also includes the rapid delivery of emergency relief supplies. Six flights have arrived at Bandaranaike International Airport, Katunayake, up until 4 December operated by the UAE Air Force, one of the world\u2019s largest cargo transport planes. The aircrafts contained temporary housing units, food packs, tents, blankets, mattresses, vehicles for rescue teams, and motorbikes designed to navigate difficult terrain. These supplies are being distributed to displaced families across severely impacted districts.\n\nThe Sri Lanka Embassy thanked the UAE\u2019s principled humanitarian policy, which emphasises swift, decisive action in times of global crisis. Rooted in a commitment to uphold human dignity, the UAE has consistently extended its hand to nations in need, regardless of geography. President Sheikh Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan has reaffirmed that the UAE stands firmly with countries confronting emergencies, pledging humanitarian aid.\n\nAs Sri Lanka battles the aftermath of its worst flooding in years, the UAE\u2019s timely intervention highlights the enduring bonds of friendship and solidarity between nations. By acting promptly and compassionately, the UAE has alleviated suffering and strengthened the spirit of resilience among those affected. The UAE\u2019s swift humanitarian response embodies the very essence of responsible and forward\u2011looking global stewardship."
