    "chunk_size_bytes": 1524,
    "chunk_text": "Very different to how politicians acted recently. The Opposition raised a furor accusing the government of not taking due notice of weather warnings. One suggestion was that wevas and reservoirs should have been carefully made to release water in view of the impending cyclone. But its path could suddenly veer from its forecast path. Then what if there is no rain? In times of national crisis, MPS should all unite, not squabble and promote individual clout: as an ex minister had gone on a food distribution campaign with his TV cameras. The affected victims had booed him off. What heartless opportunists \u2013 most politicians.\n\nBut disaster intruded. We heard of a favourite teacher\u2019s family living in Getambe losing their home and she her engagement ring and wedding clothes. She was to be married soon. Another incident was Mary\u2019s mother arriving totally distraught. Mary was a British planter\u2019s daughter with a simple Sinhala wife. He paid for Mary\u2019s education etc. The weeping woman\u2019s lament was their house was washed away. The planter was on furlough in Britain. Mary\u2019s birth secret and reason for her colour were exposed.\n\nIt was due to the small temple opposite the Getambe residence of monks being submerged in water but not damaged that conferred on it an aura of sanctity. Not one roof tile had moved out of place, From then on, this little temple had traffic stopping on their way to Kandy or leaving it. Bara \u2013 money donations -were offered to the temple to ensure the safety of the travellers."
